<title>UK: SOCCER-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONS' LEAGUE AND UEFA CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONS' LEAGUE AND UEFA CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of European Cup Champions' League second round and UEFA Cup first round, second leg matches on Wednesday:</p>
<p>UEFA Cup</p>
<p>In Cologne, Germany:</p>
<p>Borussia Moenchengladbach (Germany) 3 Arsenal (England) 2 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Moenchengladbach - Andrzej Juskowiak (23rd minute, 90th), Steffan Effenberg (75th)</p>
<p>Arsenal - Ian Wright (43rd), Paul Merson (50th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 35,000</p>
<p>Moenchengladbach won 6-4 on aggregate.  </p>
<p>UEFA Cup</p>
<p>In Tel Aviv:</p>
<p>Maccabi Tel Aviv (Israel) 1 Tenerife (Spain) 1 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Maccabi - Gadi Brumer (49th) </p>
<p>Tenerife - Angel Vivar (43rd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
<p>Tenerife won 4-3 on aggregate  </p>
<p>European Cup Champions' League</p>
<p>Group C</p>
<p>In Manchester:</p>
<p>Manchester United (England) 2 Rapid Vienna (Austria) 0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Manchester United - Ole Gunnar Solskjaer (20th), David Beckham (27th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 51,831  </p>
<p>Champions League</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>In Glasgow:</p>
<p>Glasgow Rangers (Scotland) 1 Auxerre (France) 2 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Glasgow Rangers - Paul Gascoigne (71st)</p>
<p>Auxerre - Thomas Deniaud (54th, 68th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 37,344  </p>
<p>Group C</p>
<p>In Istanbul</p>
<p>Fenerbahce (Turkey) 0 Juventus (Italy) 1</p>
<p>(halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorer: Juventus - Alen Boksic (21st minute)</p>
<p>Attendence: 28,000  </p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p>In Trondheim:</p>
<p>Rosenborg (Norway) 1 AC Milan (Italy) 4 (halftime 1-3).</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Rosenborg -Trond Egil Soltvedt (15th)</p>
<p>AC Milan - Marco Simone (6th, 23rd, 25th), George Weah (55th)</p>
<p>Attendance - 20,849  </p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>In Lodz:</p>
<p>Widzew Lodz (Poland) 1 Atletico Madrid (Spain) 4 (2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Widzew - Marek Citko (45th)</p>
<p>Atletico - Milinko Pantic (24th), Diego Simeone (32nd, 60th), Kiko (61st).  </p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>In Bucharest:</p>
<p>Steaua Bucharest (Romania) 0  Borussia Dortmund (Germany) 3 (halftime 0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Borussia Dortmund - Lars Ricken (7th), Joerg Heinrich (37th), Stephane Chapuisat (77th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000  </p>
<p>group A</p>
<p>In Amsterdam:</p>
<p>Ajax Amsterdam (Netherlands) 0 Grasshopper Zurich (Switzerland) 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Murat Yakin (58th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 42,000  </p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p>In Oporto:</p>
<p>Porto (Portugal) 2 Gothenburg (Sweden) 1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Porto - Artur Oliveira (27th, 51st)</p>
<p>Gothenburg - Jorge Costa (own goal 72nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
